    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "MECHANISM",
      "narration_text": "And there's the problem in one table. France, Germany and Italy each get a third. Every sentence it produces is perfectly fluent. Two out of three are false: Paris is the capital of Germany. The model isn't lying, and it isn't broken. It learned real patterns from true sentences. It just never learned which pairing was the fact.",
