    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "FRAMEWORK",
      "narration_text": "Real models are vastly better. They use long context, not one word, and they get Paris right. But they share the root: they're trained to predict what usually comes next. When a question lands where the patterns are thin, a rare name, a fake citation, they still produce something fluent. And they learned a confident tone too.",
